## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of cross-service orchestration with Saga patterns in a multi-tenant, event-sourced backend. It probes how to design per-tenant isolation, reliable event dispatch, and robust failure handling across regions.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant data isolation and outbox patterns
- Saga orchestration vs choreography in Event Sourcing
- Idempotent handlers, exactly-once processing, and compensations
- Observability, auditing, and retry strategies

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudo: orchestrator starts the Saga for orderId with steps
SagaContext ctx = orchestrator.startSaga(orderId, tenantId);
try {
  orchestrator.execute(ctx, List.of("Inventory", "Payment", "Shipping"));
} catch (SagaFailureException e) {
  orchestrator.compensate(ctx, reverseOrder("Inventory","Payment","Shipping"));
}
```

